A04s (Metal track M6a): preload the colour targets a fragment shader reads.

CoreAnimation's Metal renderer keeps a layer's clip and mask in a second colour attachment and reads both
attachments back in the shader (framebuffer fetch, [[color(n)]]): a draw with colour mask 0 on one target
copies it into the other, and a later draw reads that copy. libhakiosair flushes before each fetching draw
(texture_barrier), so such a draw starts a batch. Panfrost preloads a target's tile only when the batch
draws to it or has it in batch->read, and batch->read is set for depth and stencil only. A target that is
read but not written (colour mask 0) was not preloaded, the fetch read an empty tile, and on the A04s the
rounded clip's corners came out transparent and a shape mask hid its layer (run 10, scenes 3 and 4).
Mesa 25.0.7. Ours, under Mesa's licence for the file it changes (MIT).

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_cmdstream.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_cmdstream.c
@@ -2885,6 +2885,22 @@
    if (dirty & PAN_DIRTY_ZS)
       panfrost_set_batch_masks_zs(batch);
 
+   /* A04s (Metal track M6a): a fragment shader that reads a colour target
+    * (framebuffer fetch, LD_TILE) needs that target's tile preloaded even
+    * when this draw does not write it (colour mask 0). batch->read is never
+    * set for colour otherwise, so such a target was preloaded only if some
+    * draw of the batch also wrote it, and the fetch read an empty tile. */
+   {
+      const struct panfrost_compiled_shader *fs = ctx->prog[PIPE_SHADER_FRAGMENT];
+
+      if (fs && fs->info.fs.outputs_read) {
+         u_foreach_bit(i, fs->info.fs.outputs_read & BITFIELD_MASK(batch->key.nr_cbufs)) {
+            if (batch->key.cbufs[i])
+               batch->read |= PIPE_CLEAR_COLOR0 << i;
+         }
+      }
+   }
+
 #if PAN_ARCH >= 9
    if ((dirty & (PAN_DIRTY_ZS | PAN_DIRTY_RASTERIZER)) ||
        (ctx->dirty_shader[PIPE_SHADER_FRAGMENT] & PAN_DIRTY_STAGE_SHADER))
